{
    "background_story": "Axton was a self-proclaimed movie buff who spent most of his free time watching classics and new releases alike. His friends and family often joked that he had seen every film ever made. Axton's love affair with cinema began when he was a kid, sneaking into the local theater to catch matinee shows. As he grew older, his passion only intensified, and he started writing his own screenplays. After moving to Los Angeles, Axton landed a job as a film critic, attending premieres and interviewing A-list celebrities. His encyclopedic knowledge of movies earned him the nickname 'The Cinephile' among industry insiders. Axton's dream was to one day see his own film on the big screen, and with his dedication and expertise, it seemed only a matter of time before he achieved his goal.",
